Discussion

The team discussed the implementation of the Hamming (7,4) error detection algorithm in the existing MicroOS-Sim project.

The team decided to use assembly instructions for parity-bit generation and syndrome calculation. Java will be used to support the required instructions and display the error detection result.

The responsibilities were divided as follows:

* Hisham: Hamming (7,4) assembly algorithm and project integration& Documention
* Izhan: Java instruction support, including XRL and ALERT.
* Keora: Syndrome calculation and error detection testing.
* Punarvi: UI alert implementation

The team also discussed the use of XOR operations to calculate parity bits and identify incorrect bit positions.

Decisions

1. The Hamming (7,4) algorithm will be implemented using supported assembly instructions.
2. Java will provide the required XOR instruction support and output alert functionality.
3. The existing simulator functionality must be preserved.
4. Both error and no-error scenarios will be tested.
5. Each member will complete their assigned responsibilities and coordinate during integration.

